    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="0654" n="542" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg542"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/205</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Baker</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of October 29, 1919, (your File R)<anchor n="89" xml:id="d596-f1"
                    /> with reference to General Graves’
                    telegram No. 521, of October 23, 1919.<anchor n="89a" xml:id="d596-f2"/></p>
                <p>In reply thereto I beg to advise you that a cable, in substance as follows, has
                    been sent to General Graves: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Reference your No. 521, Secretary War directs that you be informed that
                            State Department has advised War Department that Omsk government warmly
                            approves your action in matter of keeping rifles from
                                Semenoff.</p>
                        <p>“State Department has requested that in future all representations to
                            Minister of Foreign Affairs at Omsk be made through Consul-General
                                Harris and not direct by
                            military authorities. Secretary War approves this request and directs
                            you take action accordingly.</p>
                        <p>“State Department advises that specific instructions have been given Mr.
                                Harris to impress upon
                            authorities at Omsk the special necessity which exists at this time for
                            a more respectful and conciliatory <pb facs="0655" n="543"
                                xml:id="pg543"/> attitude toward Americans on the part of their
                            representatives in Eastern Siberia.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Newton D.
                                Baker</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
